  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene of exaggerated frustration",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene depicted in the image, where Adolf_Hitler's intense expression and pose are used to represent the user's own exaggerated emotional reaction to seeing a gas bill. The text 'when you see the gas bill' explicitly uses the second-person pronoun 'you', directly addressing the viewer and projecting the user's experience onto the visual material of Hitler's rage. The user is not projected onto a specific textual material or visual material alone, but onto the entire scene which combines both elements to convey the user's relatable frustration.",
